guide[6][1]='For every year, solve new debt allowed by maximum opening gross debt / annual EBITDA and minimum annual EBITDA / cash interest. Use the minimum across years, capped at the committed borrowing limit. A negative underlying ratio capacity means even zero new debt fails the stated constraints.';
guide[7][1]='Interest uses opening balances. New debt repays the entered original-principal percentage annually and all remaining principal in Year 5. Existing debt follows its entered schedule. No refinancing or terminal-sale proceeds fund liquidity. Affordable EV is the minimum close and annual reserve-derived price bound at the selected committed debt and equity amounts.';
guide[8][1]='At each date, the price bound equals available buyer cash plus selected debt and equity, less close fees and investment, plus cumulative operating cash after all debt service. The minimum across close and Years 1–5 is affordable EV. The actual proposed-price cash roll-forward retains residual buyer cash. Changing the selected financing changes the bound; this is not global debt optimization.';
guide[10][1]='Standalone ceiling = PV of standalone cash and terminal EV less fees and initial investment. Add the allowed share of positive buyer synergy PV, or the full negative PV burden. Terminal EV is Year 5 standalone EBITDA, floored at zero, times the selected exit multiple. Discount year-end cash at the annual unlevered hurdle.';
